--- /dev/null
+++ b/scenes/gromen-continuous/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# The Bondfire / One System
+
+61 seconds, one Scene Plan, no reels or cuts. Individuals physically converge
+into four persistent causal groups. Packets accelerate around the same Treasury
+feedback loop; the same orb explodes and then reconstitutes during the rescue.
+The original pressure groups stay visible at the perimeter until the end.
+
+The film uses brief names and 2–5-word cues, sparse narration, optional captions,
+and no long explanatory screens. The public source bundle contains a pinned
+reproduction script and ready-made narration: no paid services are required.
+
+Run `cargo run -p psychopomp-gromen-continuous` and render `continuous.json`.
+Use `package.py` after rendering and normalizing `output/gromen-continuous-delivery.mp4`.
+`voice.py` reuses the first film's local Piper pipeline; the source bundle also
+includes that shared script for optional re-voicing.
+
+Gromen's scenario is conditional, not a forecast. Aggregation is a visual
+abstraction, not balance-sheet consolidation. Supply shocks do not mechanically
+determine real yields. Reserves are not M2; the inflationary/debasement endpoint
+is disputed. Sources and the extended discussion remain in the original artifact.
+
+Verified: all workspace tests, formatting, strict Clippy, unchanged original-film
+snapshots, deterministic continuous-scene snapshots, full-frame poses and a
+four-second 60fps grouping-motion study.
